sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Pod as GPU pod
    participant CNI as CNI
    participant SRIOV as SR-IOV / Multus
    participant NIC as RDMA NIC
    participant Peer as Peer GPU
    participant CSI as Storage
    Pod->>CNI: default cluster network
    Note over CNI: fine for control traffic, useless for collective traffic
    Pod->>SRIOV: request a second interface
    SRIOV->>NIC: attach a virtual function directly to the pod
    Pod->>NIC: NCCL all-reduce
    NIC->>Peer: RDMA — straight to GPU memory, no kernel, no copies
    Note over NIC,Peer: GPUDirect removes the bounce through host RAM entirely
    Pod->>CSI: mount the dataset
    Note over CSI,Pod: a GPU starved by slow storage is the most expensive idle resource you own
